#
# Verification masks, i.e. the regions to verify over.  MET verifies over
# each mask separately and labels the output for each with the mask's name.
# See the description of the "mask" config entry in the MET User's Guide.
#
# The METplus config variable {{METPLUS_TOOL_NAME}}_MASK_GRID sets the MET
# config entry mask.grid, a list of grids to verify over.  Each item in the
# list is usually a grid defined in MET's code, not in a file: FULL (the
# whole verification domain) or another grid built into MET, such as an
# NCEP grid named GNNN, where NNN is the 3-digit NCEP grid number (e.g.
# G212).  An item can also be a gridded data file, in which case the region
# is that file's grid.  The workflow sets {{METPLUS_TOOL_NAME}}_MASK_GRID
# (and thus mask.grid) to the names in VX_MASKS that are FULL or the name of
# a grid built into MET, in the order in which they appear there, or to
# nothing (an empty list) if there are none.  It does not pass any gridded
# data files to it.
#
# The METplus config variable {{METPLUS_TOOL_NAME}}_MASK_POLY sets the MET
# config entry mask.poly, a list of files that define verification masks.
# MET verifies over these masks in addition to the grids in mask.grid.  The
# workflow can pass two types of mask files to it: (1) lat/lon polygon
# (.poly) files, or (2) gridded mask files such as the NetCDF files made by
# MET's gen_vx_mask tool.  These files can be user-defined (in VX_MASK_DIR),
# ones that come with the workflow (in parm/metplus/vx_masks), or ones that
# come with MET (in share/met/poly).  The workflow sets
# {{METPLUS_TOOL_NAME}}_MASK_POLY (and thus mask.poly) to the files for the
# names in VX_MASKS that are names of mask files, in the order in which they
# appear there, or to nothing (an empty list) if there are none.  (See
# get_vx_mask_grids_and_files() in ush/python_utils/vx_mask_files.py for
# how each name in VX_MASKS is identified as a grid or a mask file.)
#
# {{METPLUS_TOOL_NAME}}_MASK_GRID and {{METPLUS_TOOL_NAME}}_MASK_POLY are
# the primary METplus config variables for mask.grid and mask.poly,
# respectively.  METplus also accepts other variables (aliases) that set
# mask.grid and mask.poly, but here, for clarity, we only use the primary
# variables.  If more than one METplus config variable for the same MET
# config entry is set (i.e. the primary variable and/or one or more aliases),
# METplus uses only one of them and ignores the others; their values are
# not combined, and which of these different variables comes first in the
# METplus config file does not matter (but see below if the same variable
# is set more than once).  METplus uses the first variable that is set in
# the following order, where <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME> is the tool's name in
# upper case:
#
# - Grid-Stat and Point-Stat (<METPLUS_TOOL_NAME> is GRID_STAT or
#   POINT_STAT):
#   - mask.grid:
#     1) <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_MASK_GRID
#     2) <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_GRID
#   - mask.poly:
#     1) <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_MASK_POLY
#     2) <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_VERIFICATION_MASK_TEMPLATE
#     3) <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_POLY
#
# - Ensemble-Stat (<METPLUS_TOOL_NAME> is ENSEMBLE_STAT):
#   - mask.grid:
#     1) <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_MASK_GRID (no aliases)
#   - mask.poly:
#     1) <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_MASK_POLY
#     2) <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_POLY
#     3) <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_VERIFICATION_MASK_TEMPLATE
#
# For example, for Grid-Stat, METplus first looks for
# <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_MASK_POLY in the config files.  If it is set, METplus
# passes its value to mask.poly and ignores
# <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_VERIFICATION_MASK_TEMPLATE and
# <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_POLY.  If not, METplus looks for
# <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_VERIFICATION_MASK_TEMPLATE, and if that is set, passes
# its value to mask.poly and ignores <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_POLY.  Otherwise,
# it passes the value of <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_POLY, if set, to mask.poly.
#
# A variable counts as set even if its value is empty: e.g. if
# <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_MASK_POLY is set to nothing and
# <METPLUS_TOOL_NAME>_POLY to a file, mask.poly is set to an empty list
# and the file is ignored.
#
# (If the same variable is set more than once, e.g. in two lines of one
# config file or in two config files, METplus uses the last value it reads
# and ignores the earlier ones.  This happens before the order above is
# applied.)
#
# If none of the METplus config variables for a MET config entry is set,
# METplus does not pass that entry to MET, and MET uses the value in its own
# default config file for the tool (share/met/config/<Tool>Config_default),
# which for all three tools is mask.grid = ["FULL"] and mask.poly = [] (no
# files).
#
{{METPLUS_TOOL_NAME}}_MASK_GRID = {{vx_mask_grids}}
{{METPLUS_TOOL_NAME}}_MASK_POLY = {{vx_mask_files}}
